# No Lodash

Do NOT import or use lodash in this codebase. All lodash functions have vanilla JS replacements in **@humansignal/core**.

## When you encounter or are about to write a lodash import

1. STOP — do not add any `import ... from "lodash/..."` or `require("lodash...")`
2. Use **direct subpath imports** from @humansignal/core (see below). Do not use the barrel `import { x } from "@humansignal/core"` for these utilities — use the specific module paths so the bundler resolves them correctly.
3. For cloneDeep use native `structuredClone(obj)`.

## Import paths (subpath imports)

- **debounce:** `import { debounce } from "@humansignal/core/lib/utils/debounce"`
- **String utils** (camelCase, snakeCase, kebabCase, capitalize, startCase): `import { camelCase, snakeCase, kebabCase, capitalize, startCase } from "@humansignal/core/lib/utils/string"`
- **Other utilities** (throttle, clamp, get, isMatch, uniqBy): `import { throttle, clamp, get, isMatch, uniqBy } from "@humansignal/core/lib/utils/lodash-replacements"`

## Quick reference

| Need | Import from |
|------|-------------|
| debounce | `@humansignal/core/lib/utils/debounce` |
| throttle, clamp, get, isMatch, uniqBy | `@humansignal/core/lib/utils/lodash-replacements` |
| camelCase, snakeCase, kebabCase, capitalize, startCase | `@humansignal/core/lib/utils/string` |
| cloneDeep(obj) | `structuredClone(obj)` (native) |
